Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Pick up an iPhone tonight, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.70,0:00:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,you are not holding a telephone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.41,0:00:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You are holding the most profitable consumer
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.01,0:00:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,object ever created by the human species.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.62,0:00:10.85,Default,,0,0,0,,A single block of machined
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.85,0:00:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,titanium, glass, and microscopic silicon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.08,0:00:15.29,Default,,0,0,0,,In a single ninety-day quarter, this
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.29,0:00:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,device generates more profit than Nike,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Coca-Cola, and McDonald's combined.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.70,0:00:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind that glass is a company valued
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.01,0:00:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,at more than three trillion dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.31,0:00:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,That is larger than the entire
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.18,0:00:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,gross domestic product of the United
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.06,0:00:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Kingdom, France, or India.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.93,0:00:32.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple's cash reserves could buy entire
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.42,0:00:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,airline fleets, hotel chains, or defense
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.90,0:00:37.39,Default,,0,0,0,,contractors in cash by lunchtime.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.39,0:00:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It commands a global supply
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.28,0:00:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,chain spanning six continents.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.16,0:00:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Over one billion people carry an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.90,0:00:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple device in their front pocket
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.63,0:00:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,every second of the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.37,0:00:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,When an alarm rings in Sydney,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.14,0:00:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,a podcast plays in Tokyo, or
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.92,0:00:51.70,Default,,0,0,0,,a credit card taps in London,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.70,0:00:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple takes its toll.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.47,0:00:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It has become the default operating
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.54,0:00:57.60,Default,,0,0,0,,system for modern human civilization.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.60,0:01:00.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet the entire illusion is designed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.11,0:01:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,to look effortless, friendly, and inevitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.62,0:01:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Smooth rounded corners. Minimalist packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.26,0:01:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Silk-wrapped cables. Friendly smiling typography.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.91,0:01:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the trick. Apple does
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.38,0:01:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,not sell computers. Apple sells identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.86,0:01:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It sells the flattering belief that using
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.08,0:01:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,their tools makes you a little more
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.31,0:01:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,creative, a little more rebellious, a little
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.53,0:01:23.76,Default,,0,0,0,,more special than everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.76,0:01:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It is the greatest magic
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.27,0:01:26.78,Default,,0,0,0,,trick in corporate history.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.78,0:01:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Because fifty years ago, there was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.11,0:01:31.44,Default,,0,0,0,,no glass spaceship headquarters in Cupertino.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.44,0:01:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There was no billion-dollar marketing budget. There
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.04,0:01:36.65,Default,,0,0,0,,were no clean white retail temples.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.65,0:01:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,There was only a drafty suburban
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.84,0:01:41.03,Default,,0,0,0,,garage in Los Altos, California, with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.03,0:01:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,oil stains on the concrete floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.22,0:01:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Two college dropouts who had
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.99,0:01:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,barely twenty-five dollars between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.75,0:01:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,One was an awkward, quiet engineering genius
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.30,0:01:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,who just wanted to build neat electronics.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.84,0:01:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The other was an intense, manipulative,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.26,0:01:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,barefoot college dropout who refused to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.67,0:01:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,wear shoes and ate only apples.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.09,0:02:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Wozniak built the machines. Steve Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.16,0:02:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,gave them a soul—and a price tag.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.23,0:02:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither of them knew that their
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.18,0:02:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,frantic little garage hobby was about
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.14,0:02:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,to trigger an industrial earthquake.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.09,0:02:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Nor did they know that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.66,0:02:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,the company they created would
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.22,0:02:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,one day destroy their friendship,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.79,0:02:19.44,Default,,0,0,0,,drive Jobs into public humiliation and exile,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.44,0:02:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and then, against every rule of Wall
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.85,0:02:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Street, resurrect him as the most celebrated
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.26,0:02:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate icon of the modern world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.66,0:02:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not the sanitized, polished
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.63,0:02:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,story from the keynote stage. This
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.60,0:02:32.57,Default,,0,0,0,,is the entire history of Apple.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.57,0:02:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,To understand how the fruit conquered the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.20,0:02:37.82,Default,,0,0,0,,planet, you have to rewind to 1975.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.82,0:02:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Back when computers were
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.65,0:02:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,not friendly, pocket-sized companions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.47,0:02:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,They were terrifying, multi-million-dollar behemoths locked in
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.96,0:02:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,air-conditioned basements of banks and military commands.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.46,0:02:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Run by a priesthood of men
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.95,0:02:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,in white lab coats who fed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.45,0:02:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,them paper punch cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.94,0:02:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Ordinary people were not allowed to
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.90,0:02:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,touch them. Ordinary people were supposed
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.85,0:02:58.80,Default,,0,0,0,,to be managed by them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.80,0:03:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The thought of an individual owning
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.57,0:03:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,a computer in their own house
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.34,0:03:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,was considered completely ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.10,0:03:06.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ken Olsen, the founder of
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.59,0:03:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Digital Equipment Corporation, famously declared:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.07,0:03:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,"There is no reason anyone would
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.66,0:03:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,want a computer in their home."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.24,0:03:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He was wrong. And a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.81,0:03:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,ragtag gang of California misfits
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.38,0:03:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,was about to prove it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.94,0:03:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,In Menlo Park, California, enthusiasts began gathering
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.46,0:03:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,every two weeks in a concrete garage
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.97,0:03:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,for the Homebrew Computer Club.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.48,0:03:27.61,Default,,0,0,0,,They were hobbyists, phone hackers,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.61,0:03:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,anti-war activists, and electronics geeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.74,0:03:32.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Their philosophy was simple: computers
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.76,0:03:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,should belong to the people,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.78,0:03:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,not corporations or the Pentagon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.79,0:03:39.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Among them sat twenty-four-year-old Steve
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.64,0:03:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Wozniak, an engineer at Hewlett-Packard.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.48,0:03:44.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz did not care about money,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.75,0:03:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate prestige, or conquering industries.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.02,0:03:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,He cared about engineering elegance. How to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.26,0:03:51.51,Default,,0,0,0,,do with thirty chips what other engineers
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.51,0:03:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,needed a hundred to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.76,0:03:57.05,Default,,0,0,0,,In late 1975, Woz had an epiphany.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.05,0:03:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not connect a cheap television
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.88,0:04:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,set directly to a keyboard and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.71,0:04:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,a microprocessor on a single board?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.54,0:04:04.19,Default,,0,0,0,,On a rainy Sunday in his
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.19,0:04:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,apartment, Woz typed a few keys
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.84,0:04:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,on a typewriter keyboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.49,0:04:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And for the first time in human
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.78,0:04:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,history, the letters appeared immediately on the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.06,0:04:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,television screen in front of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.35,0:04:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No punch cards. No paper printouts. No
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.50,0:04:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,waiting hours for mainframe batch processing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.64,0:04:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It was instantaneous personal computing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.33,0:04:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz was so proud that he photocopied
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.24,0:04:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,the schematics and gave them away to
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.15,0:04:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,his friends at Homebrew for free.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.06,0:04:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Deep beneath the earth in the Democratic
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.05,0:04:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Republic of Congo, children dig for cobalt.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.04,0:04:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The mineral travels across oceans
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.04,0:04:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,to chemical refineries in Asia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.05,0:04:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Before it is sealed forever into a
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.82,0:04:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,microscopic battery that powers your morning alarms.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.59,0:04:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You never see the mine. You
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.42,0:04:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,never see the cargo ship. You
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.26,0:04:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,only feel the cool glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.09,0:04:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Every swipe, every haptic tap is
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.42,0:04:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,engineered by a team of neuroscientists
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.76,0:04:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,and psychologists in Cupertino.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.10,0:05:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The notification sound—the gentle marimba chime—is recognized
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.68,0:05:04.27,Default,,0,0,0,,by more people than Beethoven's Fifth Symphony.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.27,0:05:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Before Steve and Woz built computers,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.36,0:05:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,they were outlaw telephone pirates.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.45,0:05:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz discovered that toy whistles from
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.76,0:05:13.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Cap'n Crunch cereal boxes emitted a
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.07,0:05:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,tone at exactly 2600 Hertz.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.38,0:05:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That exact frequency fooled AT&T's long-distance
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.04,0:05:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,telephone switches into granting free international
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.70,0:05:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,calls anywhere on earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.35,0:05:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,They used it to call the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.80,0:05:26.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Vatican in Rome, with Woz pretending
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.26,0:05:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,to be Henry Kissinger asking to
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.71,0:05:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,speak to the Pope.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.16,0:05:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Then twenty-year-old Steve Jobs saw
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.15,0:05:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,what Wozniak had built.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.14,0:05:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs could not design a circuit
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.61,0:05:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,board to save his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.07,0:05:39.22,Default,,0,0,0,,He did not know assembly language. But
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.22,0:05:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,he understood something infinitely rarer: human desire.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.36,0:05:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs told Wozniak to stop giving the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.55,0:05:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,designs away. 'Let's build circuit boards and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.74,0:05:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,sell them for fifty bucks.'
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.94,0:05:50.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz asked: 'What if
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.36,0:05:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,we lose our money?'
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.79,0:05:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs replied: 'At least we'll have
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.64,0:05:55.49,Default,,0,0,0,,our own company. For once in
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.49,0:05:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,our lives, we'll have a company.'
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.34,0:05:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,To raise the seed money, Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.05,0:06:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,sold his beloved Volkswagen microbus for
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.76,0:06:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,a few hundred dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.47,0:06:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Wozniak sold his prized Hewlett-Packard 65
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.16,0:06:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,scientific calculator for five hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.85,0:06:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Combined, they had thirteen hundred dollars. That
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.08,0:06:14.30,Default,,0,0,0,,was the entire capitalization of Apple Computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.30,0:06:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The name was chosen on the drive
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.26,0:06:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,back from an apple orchard commune where
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.21,0:06:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs had been pruning Gravenstein trees.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.16,0:06:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs suggested 'Apple Computer.' Woz laughed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.38,0:06:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs said it sounded fun, spirited, and
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.83,0:06:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,not intimidating. Plus, it would put them
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.29,0:06:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,ahead of Atari in the phone book.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.74,0:06:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,On April 1, 1976—April
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.25,0:06:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Fools' Day—Apple was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.76,0:06:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Their third partner, Ronald Wayne, got
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.17,0:06:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,cold feet twelve days later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.58,0:06:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,He sold his ten percent
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.15,0:06:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,stake back to Jobs and
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.72,0:06:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz for eight hundred dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.29,0:06:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, that ten percent stake would be
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.59,0:06:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,worth over three hundred billion dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.90,0:06:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs took their naked circuit board
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.41,0:06:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,to Paul Terrell, who ran the
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.92,0:06:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Byte Shop in Mountain View.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.43,0:06:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Terrell looked at it and made a
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.52,0:06:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,shocking offer: he would buy fifty units.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.61,0:07:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,But only if they were
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.46,0:07:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,fully assembled, not kit parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.30,0:07:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Price: five hundred dollars each.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.15,0:07:06.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty-five thousand dollars. It was more
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.33,0:07:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,money than either Jobs or Wozniak
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.50,0:07:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,had ever seen in their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.68,0:07:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The garage became an assembly line.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.77,0:07:14.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs's sister was paid one dollar
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.82,0:07:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,per board to solder chip sockets.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.87,0:07:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,They delivered the fifty boards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.68,0:07:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The Apple I was an
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.49,0:07:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,underground hit among hardcore hobbyists.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.30,0:07:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,They priced it at six hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.44,0:07:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,and sixty-six dollars and sixty-six cents.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.59,0:07:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Not out of satanic loyalty, but
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.70,0:07:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,because Woz liked repeating digits.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.82,0:07:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The Apple I made them fifteen
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.94,0:07:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,thousand dollars in profit. But Steve
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.07,0:07:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs was already disgusted by it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.20,0:07:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It was still just an ugly board
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.26,0:07:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,of wires. It needed a case, a
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.31,0:07:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,power supply, and a monitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.37,0:07:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs realized: true revolution wouldn't come from
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.06,0:07:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,hobbyists who knew how to solder.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.74,0:07:50.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It would come from an appliance. A
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.62,0:07:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,machine that worked straight out of the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.49,0:07:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,box, as friendly as a toaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.36,0:07:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Woz sat down and designed
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.33,0:07:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,his masterpiece: the Apple II.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.30,0:08:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a triumph of
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.77,0:08:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,engineering: color graphics, built-in sound,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.24,0:08:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,game paddles, and expansion slots.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.71,0:08:07.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs obsessed over the case. No
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.90,0:08:10.10,Default,,0,0,0,,metal screws visible. No ugly cooling
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.10,0:08:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,fan—it had to be silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.29,0:08:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,He spent weeks picking the exact
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.34,0:08:16.39,Default,,0,0,0,,warm shade of beige plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.39,0:08:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,To fund production, they needed
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.00,0:08:21.60,Default,,0,0,0,,serious capital. Enter Mike Markkula.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.60,0:08:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,A retired Intel executive who recognized
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.41,0:08:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,genius when he saw it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.22,0:08:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Markkula secured a two-hundred-and-fifty-thousand-dollar line of
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.06,0:08:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,credit and became a one-third partner.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.89,0:08:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In April 1977, Apple debuted the Apple
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.88,0:08:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,II at the West Coast Computer Faire.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.86,0:08:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,While competitors showed ugly metal boxes
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.11,0:08:41.36,Default,,0,0,0,,with exposed wires, Apple arrived like
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.36,0:08:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,a consumer company from the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.61,0:08:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,The orders poured in by the thousands.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.74,0:08:49.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Then in 1979, two Harvard programmers
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.36,0:08:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,invented VisiCalc—the world's first electronic spreadsheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.97,0:08:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Suddenly, business executives weren't buying an
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.20,0:08:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple II to play games.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.43,0:08:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,They were buying it because it could
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.25,0:09:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,do in twenty seconds what had previously
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.06,0:09:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,taken an accountant twenty hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.88,0:09:05.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The Apple II became a cash
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.15,0:09:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,printing press. Revenue exploded from eight
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.43,0:09:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,million dollars in 1978 to one
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.70,0:09:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,hundred and seventeen million in 1980.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.98,0:09:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,On December 12, 1980, Apple Computer
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.45,0:09:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,went public on Wall Street.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.92,0:09:19.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the largest public offering since
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.28,0:09:21.65,Default,,0,0,0,,the Ford Motor Company in 1956.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.65,0:09:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In an afternoon, three hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.88,0:09:26.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple employees became instant millionaires.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.11,0:09:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Jobs, at age twenty-five, was suddenly
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.88,0:09:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,worth two hundred and fifty-six million dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.66,0:09:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,He was rich, famous, and on
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.42,0:09:35.18,Default,,0,0,0,,the cover of Time magazine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.18,0:09:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He had conquered the world before his
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.12,0:09:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,hair had even begun to thin.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.05,0:09:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is when
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.24,0:09:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,the arrogance took over.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.42,0:09:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,When Steve Jobs was designing
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.35,0:09:45.28,Default,,0,0,0,,the original Apple logo, he
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.28,0:09:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,hired art director Rob Janoff.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.21,0:09:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Janoff added a single curved bite out
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.26,0:09:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,of the side so people wouldn't confuse
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.32,0:09:53.38,Default,,0,0,0,,it with a cherry or a tomato.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.38,0:09:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs added vibrant rainbow stripes
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.09,0:09:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,across the fruit to celebrate
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.80,0:09:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,the Apple II's color screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.51,0:10:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,In December 1979, Jobs made a
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.58,0:10:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,pilgrimage that changed computer history forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.66,0:10:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Xerox was a copier company whose
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.89,0:10:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate executives had funded a playground
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.12,0:10:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,of the world's greatest computer scientists.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.35,0:10:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,In exchange for a hundred thousand
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.49,0:10:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,shares of pre-IPO Apple stock, Xerox
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.62,0:10:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,agreed to open the kimono.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.76,0:10:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,They showed Jobs three technologies: object-oriented programming,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.77,0:10:25.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Ethernet networking, and the graphical user interface.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.78,0:10:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs was so blinded by the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.49,0:10:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,graphical screen with its rolling desktop
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.21,0:10:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,mouse that he barely paid attention
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.92,0:10:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,to the other two.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.64,0:10:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He watched a plastic box with
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.62,0:10:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,a rubber ball underneath move a
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.59,0:10:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,pointer smoothly across the screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.57,0:10:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He began jumping up and down
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.98,0:10:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,in the lab, shouting at the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.38,0:10:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,top of his lungs:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.79,0:10:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,"Why aren't you doing anything with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.68,0:10:46.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the greatest thing! You are
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.57,0:10:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,sitting on a gold mine!"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.46,0:10:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Xerox management was obsessed with selling
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.34,0:10:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,paper copiers. They had no idea
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.23,0:10:54.12,Default,,0,0,0,,what they had invented.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.12,0:10:56.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs ran back to Apple, assembled
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.14,0:10:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,his hardware team, and ordered them
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.16,0:11:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,to build a mouse that cost
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.19,0:11:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,fifteen dollars instead of three hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.21,0:11:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Designer Jim Hovey solved it by
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.94,0:11:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,using a rubber ball from a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.68,0:11:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,bottle of roll-on Ban deodorant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.42,0:11:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,When Jobs dropped out of Reed
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.11,0:11:10.80,Default,,0,0,0,,College, he had dropped in on
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.80,0:11:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,a calligraphy class taught by a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.49,0:11:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Trappist monk named Robert Palladino.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.18,0:11:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,He learned about serif and sans-serif
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.84,0:11:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,typefaces, varying spaces between letters, and
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.50,0:11:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,what makes great typography artistic.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.15,0:11:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Ten years later, Jobs forced
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.64,0:11:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,those fonts into the Macintosh:
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.13,0:11:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Chicago, Geneva, Venice, and Monaco.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.62,0:11:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,"If I had never dropped in on
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.85,0:11:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,that single course in college," Jobs recalled,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.08,0:11:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,"the Mac would have never had multiple
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.31,0:11:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,typefaces or proportionally spaced fonts."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.54,0:11:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs became convinced of his own infallibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.71,0:11:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,He poured tens of millions of
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.52,0:11:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,dollars into a new computer named
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.33,0:11:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,the Lisa, after his daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.14,0:11:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It was packed with revolutionary
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.26,0:11:51.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Xerox PARC graphical technology, but
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.39,0:11:53.52,Default,,0,0,0,,it cost ten thousand dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.52,0:11:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Adjusted for inflation, that is nearly thirty
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.97,0:11:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,thousand dollars for a single desk computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.42,0:12:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It flopped catastrophically. Apple ended
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.61,0:12:02.80,Default,,0,0,0,,up burying thousands of unsold
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.80,0:12:04.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Lisas in a Utah landfill.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.99,0:12:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Humiliated, the board kicked Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.04,0:12:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,off the Lisa project.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.10,0:12:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Furious, Jobs took over a small skunkworks
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.00,0:12:14.90,Default,,0,0,0,,project inside the company: the Macintosh.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.90,0:12:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,He declared war on
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.95,0:12:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,the rest of Apple.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.99,0:12:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,He hoisted a pirate flag over
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.92,0:12:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,the Macintosh building and announced:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.86,0:12:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,"It is better to be a
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.25,0:12:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,pirate than to join the Navy."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.64,0:12:26.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The Macintosh team worked ninety-hour weeks,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.14,0:12:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,fueled by fruit smoothies, espresso, and
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.63,0:12:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,fear of Jobs's blistering tantrums.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.13,0:12:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs would reduce engineers to tears, screaming
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.46,0:12:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,that their code was 'crap' or their
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.78,0:12:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,power supplies were 'too big.'
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.11,0:12:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he would return the
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.53,0:12:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,next morning and claim their
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.94,0:12:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,best idea was his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.36,0:12:44.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet they stayed. Because he pushed
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.11,0:12:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,them to do work they didn't
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.86,0:12:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,know they were capable of.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.62,0:12:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,To launch the Mac, Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.35,0:12:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,demanded a commercial unlike anything
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.09,0:12:52.82,Default,,0,0,0,,the world had ever witnessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.82,0:12:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He hired Ridley Scott, fresh
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.59,0:12:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,off directing Blade Runner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.35,0:12:58.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The commercial drew inspiration from
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.40,0:13:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,George Orwell's novel, 1984.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.46,0:13:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,IBM was cast as Big Brother, an
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.80,0:13:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,all-powerful titan commanding a brainwashed populace.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.15,0:13:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Suddenly, an athletic woman in red
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.25,0:13:11.34,Default,,0,0,0,,running shorts sprints into the hall
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.34,0:13:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,carrying a heavy sledgehammer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.44,0:13:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,She spins around and hurls the hammer
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.69,0:13:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,straight through the giant screen, exploding it
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.94,0:13:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,in a blinding flash of white light.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.18,0:13:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The voiceover declared: 'On January 24th, Apple
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.22,0:13:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Computer will introduce Macintosh. And you'll see
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.25,0:13:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,why 1984 won't be like 1984.'
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.28,0:13:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple's board of directors hated it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.31,0:13:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,They thought it was reckless, arrogant,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.34,0:13:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and insulting to IBM.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.38,0:13:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They ordered the agency to sell
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.50,0:13:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,off the Super Bowl ad time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.62,0:13:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs refused. Steve Wozniak even offered
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.75,0:13:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,to pay half the cost himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.87,0:13:47.42,Default,,0,0,0,,On Super Bowl Sunday, January 22, 1984,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.42,0:13:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,the ad aired to ninety-six million viewers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.98,0:13:53.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It aired only once on national
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.69,0:13:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,television. It changed advertising forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.40,0:13:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Two days later, Jobs walked onto the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.82,0:14:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,stage at Flint Center in Cupertino.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.25,0:14:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He wore a double-breasted suit
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.98,0:14:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,and a polka-dot bow tie.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.70,0:14:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,He pulled a small rectangular computer
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.67,0:14:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,out of a canvas carrying bag.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.64,0:14:10.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He put a floppy disk in the
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.83,0:14:13.02,Default,,0,0,0,,drive. The screen lit up. The machine
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.02,0:14:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,spoke in a synthesized voice:
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.22,0:14:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,"Hello, I am Macintosh. It sure is
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.40,0:14:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,great to get out of that bag."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.58,0:14:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The auditorium erupted into five minutes of
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.43,0:14:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,deafening standing ovations. Grown men cried.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.27,0:14:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It had a mouse. It had desktop
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.18,0:14:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,icons, windows, trash cans, and proportional fonts.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.10,0:14:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the birth of the personal
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.27,0:14:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,computer interface that every human uses today.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.44,0:14:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the hangover hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.10,0:14:41.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The Macintosh was gorgeous, but
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.06,0:14:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,it was desperately underpowered.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.03,0:14:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It had only 128 kilobytes of memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.64,0:14:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It had no hard drive. It overheated
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.25,0:14:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,because Jobs refused to install a fan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.86,0:14:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Users had to swap floppy disks
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.75,0:14:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,back and forth thirty times just
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.65,0:14:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,to copy a single file.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.54,0:14:59.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Sales hit a brick wall. By late
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.34,0:15:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,1984, Apple was producing ten thousand Macs
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.13,0:15:04.92,Default,,0,0,0,,a month and selling barely two thousand.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.92,0:15:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,The company was hemorrhaging cash.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.01,0:15:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Tensions between Jobs and CEO John
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.72,0:15:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley erupted into outright war.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.43,0:15:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs had recruited Sculley from Pepsi two
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.94,0:15:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,years earlier with the legendary challenge:
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.45,0:15:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,"Do you want to sell sugar water
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.79,0:15:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,for the rest of your life, or
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.14,0:15:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,do you want to come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.48,0:15:22.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and change the world?"
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.82,0:15:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Sculley was the one trying to
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.96,0:15:27.10,Default,,0,0,0,,rein in an out-of-control, toxic founder who
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.10,0:15:29.23,Default,,0,0,0,,terrorized employees and missed targets.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.23,0:15:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,In May 1985, Jobs plotted a palace
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.61,0:15:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,coup to remove Sculley while he was
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.98,0:15:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,on a business trip to China.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.36,0:15:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,An executive tipped Sculley off. Sculley
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.55,0:15:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,cancelled the trip and confronted Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.74,0:15:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,in a brutal boardroom showdown.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.94,0:15:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley polled the board of directors
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.83,0:15:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,one by one: 'Who do you
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.73,0:15:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,back? Me, or Steve?'
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.62,0:15:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Every single board member backed Sculley. Steve
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.43,0:15:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs was stripped of all operational authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.24,0:15:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,He was banished to an empty
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.11,0:15:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,office across the street called 'Siberia.'
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.98,0:16:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,On September 17, 1985, Steve
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.83,0:16:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs resigned from Apple.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.67,0:16:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,He sold all of his Apple
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.78,0:16:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,stock—millions of shares—keeping just one single
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.88,0:16:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,share so he could still receive
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.99,0:16:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,the annual report in the mail.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.10,0:16:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,He was thirty years old. He was
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.58,0:16:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,a multi-millionaire. And he was utterly broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.06,0:16:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs treated the Macintosh team not
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.51,0:16:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,like engineers, but like renaissance painters.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.96,0:16:25.37,Default,,0,0,0,,On February 10, 1982, Jobs gathered the
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.37,0:16:28.78,Default,,0,0,0,,entire Macintosh team for a champagne toast.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.78,0:16:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,He pulled out a large sheet of
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.86,0:16:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,drafting paper and had every single engineer
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.95,0:16:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,sign their name with a black pen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.04,0:16:37.22,Default,,0,0,0,,He then had their signatures molded
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.22,0:16:39.39,Default,,0,0,0,,permanently into the inside plastic of
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.39,0:16:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,every single Macintosh case.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.57,0:16:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,"Real artists sign their work," Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.48,0:16:45.40,Default,,0,0,0,,told them. Even though no customer
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.40,0:16:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,would ever see it unless they
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.31,0:16:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,cracked the machine open.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.22,0:16:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs obsessed over things no ordinary
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.61,0:16:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,customer would ever consciously notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.00,0:16:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,His father, Paul Jobs, a machinist, had
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.05,0:16:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,taught him: 'When you build a fence,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.09,0:17:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,you paint the back of it just
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.14,0:17:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,as well as the front.'
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.18,0:17:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs applied that ruthless aesthetic standard
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.85,0:17:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,to the Macintosh's circuit board layout.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.51,0:17:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,When John Sculley arrived from
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.13,0:17:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Pepsi, he was treated like
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.74,0:17:12.36,Default,,0,0,0,,a savior by Wall Street.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.36,0:17:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley was charismatic, polished, and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.31,0:17:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,understood mass-market consumer packaged goods.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.26,0:17:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,At first, Jobs and Sculley were inseparable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.16,0:17:24.05,Default,,0,0,0,,They called each other dynamic soulmates.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.05,0:17:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley was the adult in the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.10,0:17:28.16,Default,,0,0,0,,room who would handle operations, while
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.16,0:17:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs remained the creative lightning rod.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.22,0:17:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,But within eighteen months, the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.64,0:17:35.06,Default,,0,0,0,,relationship turned into toxic poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.06,0:17:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs blamed Sculley for pricing the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.43,0:17:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Macintosh at twenty-five hundred dollars instead
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.80,0:17:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,of two thousand, throttling early sales.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.17,0:17:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley blamed Jobs for manufacturing machines
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.66,0:17:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,that sat rotting in warehouses and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.14,0:17:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,refusing to compromise with corporate reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.63,0:17:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What followed was the wilderness decade.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.89,0:17:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,For Apple, the late 1980s started
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.34,0:17:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,smoothly on the momentum of the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.78,0:17:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Macintosh desktop publishing wave.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.23,0:18:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Aldus PageMaker, Adobe fonts, and
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.44,0:18:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,the LaserWriter made Apple the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.65,0:18:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,undisputed king of creative professionals.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.86,0:18:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Profit margins reached fifty percent. But the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.27,0:18:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,company had lost its visionary soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.68,0:18:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Under a succession of professional CEOs—John
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.27,0:18:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sculley, Michael Spindler, Gil Amelio—Apple bloated.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.86,0:18:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,They fractured the product line
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.71,0:18:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,into dozens of confusing, overlapping
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.57,0:18:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,models: Quadra, Centris, Performa, PowerBook.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.42,0:18:28.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Customers had no idea what to
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.20,0:18:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,buy. Even Apple's own salespeople could
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.98,0:18:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,not explain the difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.75,0:18:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,They burned hundreds of millions on disastrous
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.45,0:18:37.14,Default,,0,0,0,,science projects: the Newton handheld, the Pippin
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.14,0:18:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,game console, the QuickTake camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.84,0:18:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, in Redmond, Washington, an old
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.71,0:18:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,enemy was methodically sharpening his blade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.58,0:18:50.11,Default,,0,0,0,,In August 1995, Microsoft launched Windows 95.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.11,0:18:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It had a desktop, a taskbar,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.34,0:18:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,icons, windows, and a trash can.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.58,0:18:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It copied Apple's graphical interface completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.81,0:19:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It was not as elegant as the
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.66,0:19:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mac, but it was on ninety percent
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.50,0:19:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,of all personal computers on earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.35,0:19:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple's market share collapsed from sixteen
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.42,0:19:09.48,Default,,0,0,0,,percent to under four percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.48,0:19:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The company was hemorrhaging money. In 1996
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.59,0:19:15.70,Default,,0,0,0,,alone, Apple lost over one billion dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.70,0:19:18.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Worse, the aging Macintosh operating system
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.90,0:19:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,was structurally obsolete. It crashed constantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.10,0:19:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple tried and failed for
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.99,0:19:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,six years to build a
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.88,0:19:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,replacement operating system code-named Copland.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.77,0:19:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,By late 1996, Apple was
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.06,0:19:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,ninety days from formal bankruptcy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.35,0:19:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Michael Dell was publicly asked what
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.38,0:19:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,he would do if he ran
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.42,0:19:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple. His response was brutal:
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.45,0:19:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,"What would I do? I'd shut
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.90,0:19:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,it down and give the money
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.34,0:19:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,back to the shareholders."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.79,0:19:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, what had Steve Jobs been doing
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.98,0:19:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,during his eleven years in exile?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.16,0:19:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He had founded NeXT Computer, building
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.71,0:19:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,a breathtaking, magnesium-cased workstation running a
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.26,0:19:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,revolutionary Unix operating system.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.82,0:19:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a commercial failure because
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.66,0:19:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,it cost ten thousand dollars. But
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.51,0:20:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,the software was brilliant.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.36,0:20:02.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And Jobs had bought a tiny
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.58,0:20:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,computer graphics division from George Lucas
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.79,0:20:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,for five million dollars: Pixar.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.01,0:20:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,For nearly a decade, Jobs kept Pixar
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.62,0:20:12.22,Default,,0,0,0,,alive out of his own pocket, burning
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.22,0:20:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,fifty million dollars of his personal fortune.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.83,0:20:19.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Then in November 1995, Pixar released Toy
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.08,0:20:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Story—the first feature-length computer-animated film in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.33,0:20:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a global sensation. When
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.57,0:20:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Pixar went public a week later,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.82,0:20:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Jobs's eighty percent stake became
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.06,0:20:32.30,Default,,0,0,0,,worth over one billion dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.30,0:20:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He had grown up. He was
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.23,0:20:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,no longer the petulant twenty-five-year-old who
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.16,0:20:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,threw tantrums in garages.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.09,0:20:41.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He was a seasoned CEO who understood
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.40,0:20:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate governance, storytelling, and patient long-term execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.71,0:20:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,In December 1996, desperate for a
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.34,0:20:49.98,Default,,0,0,0,,new operating system, Apple CEO Gil
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.98,0:20:52.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Amelio made a fateful decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.61,0:20:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple bought NeXT for four hundred and
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.96,0:20:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,twenty-nine million dollars in cash and stock.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.31,0:20:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Jobs walked back through the
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.12,0:21:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,front doors of 1 Infinite Loop
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.93,0:21:02.74,Default,,0,0,0,,as an 'informal advisor.'
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.74,0:21:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the greatest Trojan horse in
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.16,0:21:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate history. The exile had come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.58,0:21:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,When Jobs founded NeXT in late 1985,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.78,0:21:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,he hired legendary graphic designer Paul Rand.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.97,0:21:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Rand had designed the corporate logos
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.44,0:21:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,for IBM, UPS, ABC, and Westinghouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.91,0:21:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He was seventy-one years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.38,0:21:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs asked Rand to give
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.10,0:21:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,him a few options to
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.81,0:21:26.52,Default,,0,0,0,,choose from. Rand replied bluntly:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.52,0:21:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,"No. I will solve your problem, and
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.45,0:21:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,you will pay me one hundred thousand
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.37,0:21:32.30,Default,,0,0,0,,dollars. You don't have to use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.30,0:21:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But you will pay me."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.22,0:21:37.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs paid the money. Rand delivered a
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.28,0:21:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,single design: a tilted black cube with
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.34,0:21:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,four letters: 'NeXT'. Jobs loved it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.39,0:21:46.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs spent millions perfecting the magnesium
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.26,0:21:49.14,Default,,0,0,0,,casing of the NeXT computer, insisting
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.14,0:21:52.01,Default,,0,0,0,,on perfect 90-degree internal right angles.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.01,0:21:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The computer was too expensive for
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.70,0:21:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,universities, but its software layer—NeXTSTEP—was decades
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.40,0:22:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,ahead of its time.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.10,0:22:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It was built on an
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.94,0:22:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,object-oriented language called Objective-C.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.79,0:22:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Years later, that exact software framework would
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.41,0:22:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,become the foundation of macOS, iOS, the
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.02,0:22:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,App Store, and the iPhone.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.64,0:22:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile at Pixar, an animator named
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.01,0:22:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,John Lasseter was experimenting with emotional
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.38,0:22:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,storytelling using digital algorithms.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.74,0:22:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,In 1986, they produced Luxo
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.22,0:22:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Jr.—a two-minute short film about
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.69,0:22:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,an adorable bouncing desk lamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.16,0:22:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Audiences at computer graphics conferences were moved
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.43,0:22:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,to tears by a digital lamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.70,0:22:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs realized: technology alone was cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.19,0:22:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But technology married with liberal arts
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.69,0:22:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,could touch the human soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.18,0:22:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Back in Cupertino, Apple was
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.27,0:22:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,decaying from the inside out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.36,0:22:45.91,Default,,0,0,0,,CEO Gil Amelio held bizarre, rambling keynote
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.91,0:22:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,speeches that embarrassed shareholders and exhausted employees.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.46,0:22:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Within seven months, Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.40,0:22:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,orchestrated a boardroom purge.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.33,0:22:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Gil Amelio was fired. The board was
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.58,0:22:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,overhauled. Jobs became interim CEO—the 'iCEO'—taking a
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.82,0:23:03.07,Default,,0,0,0,,salary of one dollar a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.07,0:23:05.73,Default,,0,0,0,,In August 1997, Jobs walked onto the
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.73,0:23:08.38,Default,,0,0,0,,stage at Macworld Boston. The company was
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.38,0:23:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,on the brink of death.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.04,0:23:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,He announced a shocking partnership: an
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.27,0:23:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,old nemesis was bailing them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.50,0:23:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Microsoft invested one hundred and fifty million
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.82,0:23:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,dollars in non-voting Apple stock and guaranteed
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.13,0:23:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Office on Mac for five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.44,0:23:25.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The audience booed. Jobs stopped them cold
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.09,0:23:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,with a line of devastating pragmatism:
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.74,0:23:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,"We have to let go of
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.51,0:23:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,this notion that for Apple to
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.27,0:23:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,win, Microsoft has to lose. For
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.03,0:23:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple to win, Apple has to
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.79,0:23:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,do a really good job."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.55,0:23:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he took a black marker and
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.58,0:23:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,marched into the product development room.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.61,0:23:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He drew a simple two-by-two
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.12,0:23:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,grid on the whiteboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.63,0:23:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,"Here is what we need: four
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.12,0:23:48.61,Default,,0,0,0,,great products. Two for professionals, two
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.61,0:23:51.10,Default,,0,0,0,,for consumers. Everything else, we cancel."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.10,0:23:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,He eliminated seventy percent of
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.18,0:23:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple's product line overnight. Three
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.27,0:23:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,thousand employees were laid off.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.36,0:23:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,He walked into Apple's design studio
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.45,0:24:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and found a young, soft-spoken British
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.54,0:24:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,designer named Jony Ive.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.62,0:24:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs recognized an artistic soulmate. Together,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.53,0:24:09.43,Default,,0,0,0,,they began redesigning the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.43,0:24:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,In May 1998, Jobs unveiled the machine
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.58,0:24:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,that saved Apple: the iMac G3.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.72,0:24:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It was translucent Bondi blue. It had
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.06,0:24:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,a handle on top. It threw away
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.39,0:24:22.73,Default,,0,0,0,,the floppy drive and embraced USB.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.73,0:24:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,PC makers laughed. But the iMac became
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.36,0:24:27.98,Default,,0,0,0,,the fastest-selling computer in Apple's history.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.98,0:24:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple turned an eighty-seven-million-dollar profit in its
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.73,0:24:33.48,Default,,0,0,0,,first full year under Jobs's return.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.48,0:24:35.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Then came the defining shift:
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.57,0:24:37.66,Default,,0,0,0,,the digital hub strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.66,0:24:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs realized the personal computer was no
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.95,0:24:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,longer just for word processing. It was
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.25,0:24:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,the command center for a digital lifestyle.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.54,0:24:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,In October 2001, six weeks
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.82,0:24:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,after 9/11, Jobs held a
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.09,0:24:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,low-key press conference in Cupertino.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.36,0:24:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He reached into his pocket and pulled
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.62,0:24:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,out a sleek stainless-steel device the size
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.87,0:24:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,of a deck of cards: the iPod.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.13,0:25:00.70,Default,,0,0,0,,His pitch was an absolute masterpiece of
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.70,0:25:03.26,Default,,0,0,0,,copywriting: 'One thousand songs in your pocket.'
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.26,0:25:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,During development, an engineer insisted the prototype
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.89,0:25:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,was as compact as physically possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.52,0:25:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs walked over to an office aquarium
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.64,0:25:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,and dropped the iPod into the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.77,0:25:14.84,Default,,0,0,0,,As it sank, bubbles floated to
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.84,0:25:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,the surface. Jobs said: 'Those are
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.92,0:25:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,air bubbles. That means there's empty
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.00,0:25:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,space. Make it smaller.'
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.07,0:25:23.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The iPod conquered the music industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.76,0:25:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2003, Apple launched the iTunes Music
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.90,0:25:30.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Store, selling songs for ninety-nine cents.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.05,0:25:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The record labels, terrified of
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.18,0:25:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Napster and internet piracy, surrendered
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.32,0:25:36.46,Default,,0,0,0,,their catalog to Steve Jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.46,0:25:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple was no longer a computer company.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.75,0:25:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a digital culture company.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.04,0:25:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Over four hundred million iPods were
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.39,0:25:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,sold. But Jobs wasn't satisfied.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.74,0:25:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,He looked at mobile cellphones and
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.56,0:25:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,saw clunky, hideous plastic bricks covered
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.38,0:25:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,in tiny plastic buttons.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.19,0:25:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He hated every single one of
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.88,0:25:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,them. 'Everyone hates their phone,' he
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.57,0:25:56.26,Default,,0,0,0,,told his executive team.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.26,0:25:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,He also realized something terrifying:
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.67,0:26:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,if cellphones learned to play
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.09,0:26:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,MP3s, the iPod would die.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.50,0:26:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,"If we don't cannibalize ourselves,"
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.50,0:26:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs warned, "someone else will."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.49,0:26:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,For two secret years, Apple's finest
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.78,0:26:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,hardware and software engineers labored in
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.08,0:26:14.38,Default,,0,0,0,,lockdown mode on Project Purple.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.38,0:26:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They invented multi-touch technology: the ability to
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.13,0:26:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,swipe, pinch, and zoom on a sheet
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.88,0:26:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,of pure glass with human fingertips.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.63,0:26:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,On January 9, 2007, Steve Jobs took
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.58,0:26:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,the stage at Macworld San Francisco.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.54,0:26:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the greatest product introduction
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.29,0:26:32.04,Default,,0,0,0,,in the history of business.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.04,0:26:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"Every once in a while,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.01,0:26:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,a revolutionary product comes along
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.98,0:26:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,that changes everything," Jobs began.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.94,0:26:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,"Today, we are introducing three
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.18,0:26:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,revolutionary products of this class."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.41,0:26:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,"The first one is a widescreen
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.50,0:26:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,iPod with touch controls. The second
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.60,0:26:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,is a revolutionary mobile phone."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.70,0:26:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,"And the third is a
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.40,0:26:52.10,Default,,0,0,0,,breakthrough internet communications device."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.10,0:26:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,"An iPod. A phone. And an
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.82,0:26:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,internet communicator. Are you getting it?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.53,0:27:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,These are not three separate devices."
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.24,0:27:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,"This is one device. And
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.09,0:27:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,we are calling it: iPhone."
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.94,0:27:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The demo was a technological tightrope
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.05,0:27:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,walk. The phone barely worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.16,0:27:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The operating system had memory leaks. If
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.49,0:27:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs clicked icons in the wrong order,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.82,0:27:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,the phone would crash completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.14,0:27:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs performed the forty-five-minute demonstration with absolute
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.73,0:27:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,flawless perfection. Not a single glitch occurred.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.32,0:27:24.54,Default,,0,0,0,,When Steve Jobs stepped off that
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.54,0:27:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,stage, the entire mobile industry had
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.75,0:27:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,been rendered obsolete in forty-five minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.97,0:27:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The CEO of BlackBerry dismissed it,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.08,0:27:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,saying enterprise customers would never buy
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.19,0:27:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,a phone without a physical keyboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.30,0:27:38.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Ballmer, CEO of Microsoft, literally
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.26,0:27:41.21,Default,,0,0,0,,laughed out loud on national television:
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.21,0:27:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Five hundred dollars fully subsidized? It is
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.98,0:27:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,the most expensive phone in the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.74,0:27:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,and it doesn't appeal to business customers!"
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.51,0:27:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Within five years, BlackBerry was
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.57,0:27:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,virtually wiped off the map.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.62,0:27:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Nokia's mobile business was incinerated.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.68,0:27:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And Apple became the most valuable technology
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.71,0:27:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,company on the face of the earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.74,0:28:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2008, Apple launched the App
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.16,0:28:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Store with just five hundred apps.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.58,0:28:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It unlocked an entirely new global digital
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.65,0:28:12.72,Default,,0,0,0,,economy: Uber, Instagram, WhatsApp, Airbnb, DoorDash.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.72,0:28:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple took thirty percent of every
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.69,0:28:16.66,Default,,0,0,0,,transaction. It was a digital toll
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.66,0:28:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,road on human culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.62,0:28:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Then came the iPad in
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.96,0:28:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,2010. The MacBooks with unibody
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.30,0:28:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,aluminum. The custom silicon chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.63,0:28:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,When Jobs returned to Apple in
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.72,0:28:29.81,Default,,0,0,0,,1997, his first television commercial was
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.81,0:28:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,not about computers at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.90,0:28:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a sixty-second tribute to
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.56,0:28:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,the troublemakers and the misfits.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.23,0:28:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,"Here's to the crazy ones," the narration
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.18,0:28:41.14,Default,,0,0,0,,began. "The misfits. The rebels. The troublemakers.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.14,0:28:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The round pegs in the square holes."
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.09,0:28:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,"Because the people who are crazy enough
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.78,0:28:47.48,Default,,0,0,0,,to think they can change the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.48,0:28:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,are the ones who do."
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.18,0:28:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It didn't sell megahertz or gigabytes.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.41,0:28:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It re-established Apple as the brand
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.64,0:28:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,for dreamers and creators.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.87,0:28:57.73,Default,,0,0,0,,When Jobs and his software
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.73,0:28:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,engineers designed Mac OS X,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.58,0:29:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,they created the Aqua interface.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.44,0:29:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs boasted to reporters: "We made the
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.46,0:29:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,buttons on the screen look so good
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.47,0:29:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll want to lick them."
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.49,0:29:09.94,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2001, every retail expert told
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.94,0:29:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs that building brick-and-mortar stores would
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.38,0:29:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,be an expensive suicide mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.83,0:29:17.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Gateway was closing its stores. Dell
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.34,0:29:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,was selling exclusively online. Conventional wisdom
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.86,0:29:22.37,Default,,0,0,0,,said physical retail was dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.37,0:29:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs hired Mickey Drexler from Gap
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.66,0:29:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,and built a secret prototype store
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.96,0:29:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,inside an empty warehouse in Cupertino.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.26,0:29:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,He insisted on genuine Italian pietra
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.77,0:29:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,serena sandstone for the floors, quarried
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.28,0:29:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,from a family-owned hillside in Florence.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.79,0:29:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He patented the iconic spiral glass staircases,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.14,0:29:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,testing each floating glass tread to hold
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.50,0:29:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,the weight of an elephant.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.85,0:29:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The Genius Bar replaced traditional
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.70,0:29:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,cash registers with friendly experts
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.54,0:29:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,who fixed problems for free.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.39,0:29:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple Stores became the most profitable
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.41,0:29:53.42,Default,,0,0,0,,retail spaces per square foot in
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.42,0:29:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,the history of global commerce.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.44,0:29:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Six months before the iPhone launched, Steve
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.61,0:30:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs made a furious discovery during testing.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.78,0:30:03.95,Default,,0,0,0,,He carried the prototype in his pocket
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.95,0:30:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,with his car keys. The plastic screen
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.13,0:30:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,was completely covered in scratches.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.30,0:30:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,"I won't sell a product that
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.24,0:30:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,gets scratched," Jobs raged. "I want
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.17,0:30:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,a glass screen. And I want
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.10,0:30:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,it perfect in six months."
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.03,0:30:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He called Wendell Weeks, the CEO
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.23,0:30:20.44,Default,,0,0,0,,of Corning Glass, who had an
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.44,0:30:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,experimental glass recipe invented in the
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.64,0:30:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,1960s called 'Gorilla Glass.'
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.84,0:30:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind the triumph, Steve Jobs was dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.25,0:30:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He had battled pancreatic cancer
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.88,0:30:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,for eight grueling years.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.51,0:30:34.10,Default,,0,0,0,,In August 2011, knowing the end was
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.10,0:30:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,near, Jobs resigned as CEO and handed
Dialogue: 0,0:30:36.70,0:30:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,the reins to his COO: Tim Cook.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.29,0:30:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Cook was an Alabama-born supply chain savant.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.24,0:30:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Low-key, methodical, disciplined, and utterly unpretentious.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.18,0:30:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs's final advice to Cook was
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.08,0:30:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,simple: 'Never ask what I would
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.98,0:30:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,do. Just do what's right.'
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.87,0:30:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,On October 5, 2011, Steve Jobs
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.17,0:30:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,passed away at his home in
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.46,0:30:59.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Palo Alto at age fifty-six.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.76,0:31:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Across the globe, Apple retail
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.99,0:31:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,stores became spontaneous shrines.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.22,0:31:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Mourners left real apples with bite marks
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.46,0:31:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,taken out of them on the sidewalks.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.69,0:31:12.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Wall Street predicted Apple's doom. 'Without Jobs's
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.22,0:31:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,creative genius,' critics wrote, 'Apple will fade.'
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.74,0:31:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,They were catastrophically wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.81,0:31:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Tim Cook did not try to be
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.14,0:31:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,a rockstar visionary. He turned Apple into
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.46,0:31:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,the most efficient manufacturing engine on earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.79,0:31:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,He launched the Apple Watch, dominating
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.16,0:31:29.52,Default,,0,0,0,,the entire luxury timepiece industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.52,0:31:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He launched AirPods, which by themselves make
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.41,0:31:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,more revenue than most Fortune 500 corporations.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.30,0:31:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,He built Apple Silicon—the M1 and M-series
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.80,0:31:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,chips—blowing Intel's processors out of the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.29,0:31:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,In August 2018, Apple became the
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.86,0:31:47.42,Default,,0,0,0,,first public American company in history
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.42,0:31:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,to reach a one-trillion-dollar valuation.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.99,0:31:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Two years later, it hit
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.56,0:31:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,two trillion. Then, three trillion.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.13,0:31:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Under Tim Cook, Apple created
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.38,0:31:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,more shareholder wealth than any
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.62,0:32:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,corporate entity in human history.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.87,0:32:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet with ungodly scale came
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.90,0:32:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,an unavoidable moral reckoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.93,0:32:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,In Zhengzhou, China—known as 'iPhone City'—over
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.58,0:32:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,two hundred thousand factory workers assemble
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.22,0:32:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,devices on grueling twelve-hour shifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.87,0:32:19.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Anti-suicide nets had to be strung along
Dialogue: 0,0:32:19.60,0:32:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,factory dormitories to catch exhausted workers.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.32,0:32:24.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Developers sued Apple over the thirty
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.41,0:32:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,percent App Store 'tax,' comparing the
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.50,0:32:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,walled garden to a feudal monopoly.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.58,0:32:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,The European Union forced Apple to
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.74,0:32:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,abandon its proprietary Lightning cable in
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.89,0:32:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,favor of universal USB-C.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.04,0:32:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Governments around the world launched antitrust
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.87,0:32:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,probes, accusing Apple of suffocating competition
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.70,0:32:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and locking users in digital handcuffs.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.54,0:32:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And millions of parents began noticing
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.58,0:32:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that their children couldn't look away
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.63,0:32:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,from the little glowing glass rectangles.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.68,0:32:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The company that promised to free humans
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.67,0:32:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,from the totalitarian machine in 1984 had
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.66,0:32:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,built its own inescapable digital cage.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.66,0:33:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It was comfortable. It was beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.90,0:33:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,And nobody wanted to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.14,0:33:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,In 1976, two broke kids in
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.44,0:33:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,a drafty garage started building circuit
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.73,0:33:10.02,Default,,0,0,0,,boards because they thought technology should
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.02,0:33:12.31,Default,,0,0,0,,belong to the individual.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.31,0:33:15.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, their creation governs the communications,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.08,0:33:17.85,Default,,0,0,0,,finances, entertainment, and memories of over
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.85,0:33:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,a billion human beings.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.62,0:33:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,They gave humanity a
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.90,0:33:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,bicycle for the mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.18,0:33:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The only question left is
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.55,0:33:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,who is really riding whom.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.92,0:33:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,From an unpainted garage in Los
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.43,0:33:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Altos to a three-trillion-dollar glass empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.94,0:33:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for building
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.09,0:33:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,this story with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.24,0:33:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,If you felt the spark of
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.08,0:33:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,this story, hit like and subscribe
Dialogue: 0,0:33:36.91,0:33:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,for the complete history of more
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.75,0:33:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,empires, one founder at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.58,0:33:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And tell us in the comments below:
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.82,0:33:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,what was the very first Apple product
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.05,0:33:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,you ever held in your hands? The
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.28,0:33:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,II, the iPod, or the iPhone?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.51,0:33:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,See you at the next build.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.81,0:33:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Corning had never manufactured Gorilla Glass
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.86,0:33:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,in mass quantities. Weeks said it
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.90,0:33:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,would take years to scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.95,0:33:58.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Jobs replied: "Don't be afraid. You
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.94,0:34:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,can do this. Get your mind
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.92,0:34:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,around it." Within six months, Corning
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.91,0:34:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,converted an entire factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.90,0:34:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,When the first iPhone shipped on
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.41,0:34:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,June 29, 2007, it had a
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.92,0:34:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,flawless, diamond-hard Gorilla Glass display.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.43,0:34:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When Tim Cook took over,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:14.58,0:34:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,he quietly revolutionized corporate operations.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.73,0:34:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Cook eliminated Apple's owned warehouses, slashing inventory
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.75,0:34:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,holding time from months to just hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.78,0:34:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,If a computer part sat on a
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.66,0:34:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,shelf for three days, Cook considered it
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.55,0:34:28.44,Default,,0,0,0,,a criminal waste of capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.44,0:34:31.45,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2019, Apple introduced the Apple Card,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.45,0:34:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,crafted out of laser-etched pure titanium.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.46,0:34:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2023, Apple unveiled the
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.60,0:34:38.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Vision Pro, attempting to replace
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.74,0:34:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,flat screens with spatial computing.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.87,0:34:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,From room-sized mainframe computers to personal
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.82,0:34:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,computers, to pocket screens, to computers
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.78,0:34:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,strapped directly to human faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.73,0:34:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The trajectory has always been the
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.94,0:34:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,same: moving the digital world closer
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.14,0:34:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and closer to human consciousness.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.35,0:34:57.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Steve Jobs once said that
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.85,0:34:59.34,Default,,0,0,0,,computers were the equivalent of
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.34,0:35:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,a bicycle for our minds.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.84,0:35:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Fifty years later, that bicycle has carried
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.62,0:35:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple into the stratosphere of human civilization.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.41,0:35:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,A company built by outcasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.40,0:35:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,pirates, and dreamers who believed
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.39,0:35:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,they could dent the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.38,0:35:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And against every rational probability
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.63,0:35:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,in corporate history, they did.